# OODA Zero-Trust Surface — CapReg64 & Bare-Metal oodar

File: linguist/samples/OODA/capreg64_oodar.oot

`CapReg64` is the single-cycle 64-bit capability register: the lower 32
bits say **WHAT** (one bit per explicit capability, `0..31`), the upper
32 bits say **HOW/WHEN**. A null register fails closed; there is no
ambient authority anywhere in `oostd` or `oodar`.

## Register layout

```text
[63:48] epoch16  |  [47:40] rights8  |  [39:32] badge8  |  [31:0] caps32
```

The 32 explicit capabilities split into 19 software/OS bits (`NetCap`,
`ProcessCap`, `FsWriteCap`, `FsReadCap`, `SysCap`, `FsCap`, `TimeCap`,
`RandCap`, `AllocCap`, `ArenaCap`, `FfiCap`, `MetricsCap`, `SignCap`,
`TcpCap`/`TlsCap`, `UdpCap`, `BindCap`, `ThreadCap`, `EnvCap`,
`CompilerReadCap`) and 13 hardware bits (`MmioCap`, `DmaCap`, `IrqCap`,
`PciCap`, `AudioCap`, `CameraCap`, `UsbCap`, `HidCap`, `WindowCap`,
`FrameCap`, `GpuCap`, `BlockCap`, `TpmCap`).

## The fail-closed admit gate

`cap_admit` is the canonical gate shape: `-13` on a null register, `-22`
on out-of-field-width args checked BEFORE the masking call (a
`req_rights` of `999` would silently narrow to `231` and wrongly pass),
`-13` on `oo_cap_reg64_check` failure, `0` on admit. `req_caps` is
hoisted into a `let` so the compiler counts arguments correctly.

```oo
fn cap_admit(reg64: Int, epoch: Int, req_rights: Int) -> Int {
    let req_caps: Int = 1 << oo_cap_bit_index("FsReadCap");
    if reg64 == 0 { return -13; }
    if epoch < 0 || req_rights < 0 || req_rights > 255 { return -22; }
    if !oo_cap_reg64_check(reg64, epoch, req_rights, req_caps) { return -13; }
    return 0;
}
```

`oo_cap_reg64_attenuate` then restricts a parent register monotonically
for child delegation; `oo_cap_privacy_attenuate` additionally strips
network, camera, mic, and frame bits for privacy handoffs.

## Bare-metal oodar substrate

The `nostd` path of `liboodar.a` exports the freestanding veneers:
`oo_mmio_read8/16/32/64`, `oo_mmio_write8/16/32/64`, `oo_mmio_barrier`,
`oo_nostd_uart_init/read/write`, `oo_nostd_arena_init`,
`oo_nostd_alloc`, `oo_nostd_cap_mask`, `oo_nostd_abort`,
`oo_nostd_panic`. Every veneer takes an explicit token; a forged or
missing token aborts at the cap check.

```oo
pub fn uart_putc(reg64: Int, epoch: Int, ch: Int) -> Int {
    if uart_hw_admit(reg64, epoch) != 0 { return -13; }
    while (oo_mmio_read8(536936452) & 32) == 0 { oo_mmio_barrier(); }
    oo_mmio_write8(536936448, ch & 255);
    return 0;
}
```

See `capreg_attenuation.oo` and `bare_metal_oodar.oo` for the full pages.
